In the extortion emails heise sampled, a so far rather unknown gang calling itself "LPG Group" claims responsibility for the acts, while heise describes the intruders as criminals unknown until now ([heise online, 2026-09-26](https://www.heise.de/news/Kunden-und-Mitarbeiter-von-Lieferdienst-Flink-werden-erpresst-11467086.html)). According to Flink, the abuse report to the group's mail provider has curbed the flood of emails only for now, and it cannot be ruled out that the extortionists will look for other routes ([heise online, 2026-09-26](https://www.heise.de/news/Kunden-und-Mitarbeiter-von-Lieferdienst-Flink-werden-erpresst-11467086.html)).
